# Verdict notes (2026-08-11, feature/element-cow-hs):
# midfile-corrupt/recovery-rate REDpending(T6): resync recovered 90135 < synced 180000
# — the good tail behind the mid-file splice did not resync (recovered ≈ front half).
# First occurrence of this cell flaking. Evidence for flake, not regression:
#   - diff under test touches kevy-store collection encodings only; the cell's
#     workload is strings-only (crash_writer SET loop) and the resync scanner
#     (kevy-persist replay) is untouched by the branch.
#   - local run on the same tree: recovery-rate PASS (91500 >= 91500).
#   - CI rerun of the same commit: PASS.
# Mechanism hypothesis: the 7-byte splice at size/2 is position-dependent —
# values are uniform 'b' runs, and an unlucky offset can leave the forward
# scanner without a recoverable frame boundary lock. Recurs => instrument the
# resync scanner with the splice offset and dig per the flake discipline.
